It is Thursday evening, half past five.
I am in the sports hall at badminton.
Usually, I go to the reception first.
I rent a racket, because I do not have one.
Timo, Lena, and Max are already standing on the court.
"Hello everyone, how are you?" I ask.
"Good, but we are very hot!" Lena answers.
It is summer and the air in the hall is extremely warm.
We are playing doubles today: Timo and I against Lena and Max.
The game is fast and very exhausting.
"Are you already tired?" I call after fifteen minutes.
Max laughs out loud and shakes his head.
Mostly we take a short break after a game.
We stand together at the edge and drink water.
Fortunately, a large window is opened.
A little bit of fresh air comes in.
That feels good, and we keep playing right away.
